That's wonderful to hear that "What was one good thing today? Tell me more!" helped last night. It sounds like Noa was able to share about the frog he saw at daycare.

For a 4-year-old, continuing to build on that connection and communication is great. One possibility for what's next could be to try asking about "one good thing" earlier in the day, maybe when you pick him up or right after he gets home, to see if that changes what he shares. This is a gentle way to keep encouraging his verbal expression and connection.

